irs between two or more things, persisting statically over some time interval. IE, a state of the world.'}, {'subject': 'black', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:Thing'}, {'subject': 'isNextTo', 'predicate': 'rdfs:label', 'object': 'am next to'}, {'subject': 'cyc:FluidTangibleThing', 'predicate': 'rdfs:label', 'object': 'fluide'}, {'subject': 'cyc:SpatialThing', 'predicate': 'rdfs:label', 'object': 'spatial thing'}, {'subject': 'dbr:Bed', 'predicate': 'cocoClass', 'object': 'bed'}, {'subject': 'cyc:doneBy', 'predicate': 'rdfs:comment', 'object': 'A very general predicate that relates events to the things that "do" them. (doneBy EVENT DOER) means that DOER is a "doer" in the event EVENT: some activity on the part of DOER causes or carries out EVENT. This predicate is agnostic as to whether DOER does EVENT intentionally or not. Note that DOER need not even be animate or an agent; e.g. the famous vocanic eruption that buried Pompeii was doneBy Mt. Vesuvius. Note also that an event might have more than one doer; consider a chess game.'}, {'subject': 'Cardboardbox', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:Thing'}, {'subject': 'RightHand', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:Thing'}, {'subject': 'isSharedSituation', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:Thing'}, {'subject': 'isAbleTo', 'predicate': 'rdfs:label', 'object': 'am able to'}, {'subject': 'isAbove', 'predicate': 'owl:inverseOf', 'object': 'isBelow'}, {'subject': 'cyc:above_Touching', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:ObjectProperty'}, {'subject': 'NonAlcoholicBeverage', 'predicate': 'rdfs:subClassOf', 'object': 'cyc:Drink'}, {'subject': 'cyc:Resting-Relaxing', 'predicate': 'rdfs:comment', 'object': 'The collection of events in which an animal abstains from strenuous physical activity.'}, {'subject': 'dbr:Orange_(fruit)', 'predicate': 'cocoClass', 'object': 'orange'}, {'subject': 'cyc:Can', 'predicate': 'openCycUri', 'object': 'http://sw.opencyc.org/concept/Mx4rvVj-85wpEbGdrcN5Y29ycA'}, {'subje