ther spatial objects (see SpaceRegion). An important specialization of EnduringThing_Localized is Place (q.v.). The salient distinction between places (instances of Place) and locations (instances of EnduringThing_Localized) is that places are assumed to have relatively permanent locations, whereas locations need not have permanent locations. Thus, from the perspective of someone standing on a beach, the crest of a breaking wave can be a location at which foaming is occuring (thus an EnduringThing_Localized), but it cannot be such a place (i.e. it cannot be an instance of Place).'}, {'subject': 'currentlyDoneBy', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:ObjectProperty'}, {'subject': 'cyc:holds-Underspecified', 'predicate': 'rdfs:range', 'object': 'owl:Thing'}, {'subject': 'cyc:Food', 'predicate': 'rdfs:subClassOf', 'object': 'cyc:FoodOrDrink'}, {'subject': 'hasPosture', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:FunctionalProperty'}, {'subject': 'contains', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:ObjectProperty'}, {'subject': 'dbr:Apple', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:Thing'}, {'subject': 'TimeInterval', 'predicate': 'rdfs:label', 'object': 'time interval'}, {'subject': 'pointsAt', 'predicate': 'rdfs:range', 'object': 'cyc:EnduringThing-Localized'}, {'subject': 'hasShape', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:Thing'}, {'subject': 'hasGoal', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:Thing'}, {'subject': 'cyc:Can', 'predicate': 'rdfs:subClassOf', 'object': 'Artifact'}, {'subject': 'cyc:FurniturePiece', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:Thing'}, {'subject': 'ToyCube', 'predicate': 'rdfs:subClassOf', 'object': 'dbr:Toy'}, {'subject': 'Robot', 'predicate': 'openCycUri', 'object': 'http://sw.opencyc.org/concept/Mx4rwQr1pJwpEbGdrcN5Y29ycA'}, {'subject': 'dbr:Laptop', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:Thing'}, {'subject': 'Shelf', 'predicate': 'rdfs:label', 'object': 'shelf'}, {'subject': 'leftOf', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:TransitivePropert