lative location'}, {'subject': 'Jacket', 'predicate': 'rdfs:subClassOf', 'object': 'Cloth'}, {'subject': 'Shelf', 'predicate': 'rdfs:label', 'object': 'étagère'}, {'subject': 'jointEngagementWith', 'predicate': 'rdfs:comment', 'object': 'describes that two situations experiences by two agents are in fact mutual engagement (ie, the two situations are EngagementSituations, and the two agents are engaged together).\n\n?a experiences ?s1, ?b experiences ?s2, ?s1 jointEngagementWith ?s2 implies that ?s1 and ?s2 are engagement situations experienced by ?a and ?b, and ?a and ?b are in fact engaged together.'}, {'subject': 'cyc:Action', 'predicate': 'rdfs:comment', 'object': 'An action implies several thematic roles (or semantic roles):\n\nWe use this list of roles (Aarts 1997: 88), which are mapped to specific predicates :\nAgent: The ‘doer’ or instigator of the action denoted by the predicate.\nPatient: The ‘undergoer’ of the action or event denoted by the predicate.\nTheme: The entity that is moved by the action or event denoted by the predicate.\nExperiencer: The living entity that experiences the action or event denoted by the predicate.\nGoal: The location or entity in the direction of which something moves.\nBenefactive: The entity that benefits from the action or event denoted by the predicate.\nSource: The location or entity from which something moves\nInstrument: The medium by which the action or event denoted by the predicate is carried out.\nLocative: The specification of the place where the action or event denoted by the predicate in situated.'}, {'subject': 'dbr:Teddy_bear', 'predicate': 'cocoClass', 'object': 'teddy bear'}, {'subject': 'dbr:Teddy_bear', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:Thing'}, {'subject': 'hasColor', 'predicate': 'rdfs:subPropertyOf', 'object': 'hasFeature'}, {'subject': 'myself', 'predicate': 'rdfs:label', 'object': 'myself'}, {'subject': 'dbr:Cabinetry', 'predicate': 'rdfs:label', 'object': 'cabinet'}, {'subject': 'RegionOfSpace', 'predicate': 'owl:equivalentClass', 'object': 'cyc:SpaceRegion'}, {'subject': 'dbr:Spoon', 'predicate': 'cocoClass', 'object': 'spoon'}, {'subject': 'foaf:knows', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:ObjectProperty'}, {'subject': 'cylinderShape', 'predicate': 'rdfs:label', 'object': 'cylindrique'}, {'subject': 'Cloth', 'predicate': 'rdfs:subClassOf', 'object': 'cyc:SolidTangibleThing'}, {'subject': 'blue', 'predicate': 'rdfs:label', 'object': 'bleu'}, {'subject': 'EmotionalState', 'predicate': 'rdfs:comment', 'object': 'Describes the emotional state of an agent, like being happy, confused, sad...'}, {'subject': 'inFrontOf', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:ObjectProperty'}, {'subject': 'cyc:PurposefulAction', 'predicate': 'rdfs:comment', 'object': 'A specialization of both Action and AtLeastPartiallyMentalEvent. Each instance of PurposefulAction is an action consciously, volitionally, and purposefully done by (see performedBy) at least one actor.'}, {'subject': 'preferredName', 'predicate': 'rdfs:comment', 'object': 'Preferred name of an agent. If the agent has other names, the can be access via hasName.'}, {'subject': 'SpaceChunk', 'predicate': 'rdfs:subClassOf', 'object': 'cyc:SpaceRegion'}, {'subject': 'Uncover', 'predicate': 'rdfs:subClassOf', 'object': 'Manipulation'}, {'subject': 'duration', 'predicate': 'rdfs:domain', 'object': 'cyc:TemporalThing'}, {'subject': 'Jacket', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:Class'}, {'subject': 'ZoneOfAction', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:Thing'}, {'subject': 'dbr:Knife', 'predicate': 'cocoClass', 'object': 'knife'}, {'subject': 'Point', 'predicate': 'rdfs:comment', 'object': 'For ease of use, we use here "Point" as "Point-Empirical" in the Open Cyc ontology. The OpenCyc URI refers to the correct one ("Point-Empirical")'}, {'subject': 'owl:Thing', 'predicate': 'rdf:type', 'object': 'owl:Class'}, {'subject': 'currentlyPerforms', 'predicate': 'rdfs:comment', 'object': '(currentlyPerforms AGENT ACTION) mea